        b.AppendLine("Canonical authority: [`"+V2Crosswalk+"`]("+V2Crosswalk+") and [`"+V2Reconciliation+"`]("+V2Reconciliation+"). v1 is superseded and retained unchanged, together with its complete 52-file attempt. No product/history source was changed.\n");
        b.AppendLine("The v1 mapper accepted family/file-wide lists and generic constructor-name matches. Referential integrity alone did not establish semantic lineage. v2 removes that fallback: each non-exact historical ID has a reviewed operation recipe, historical body SHA proof, a unique current declaration selector, exact operation anchors, and accepted-batch body/ancestry proof. Context-existing providers are separated from operations that actually moved.\n");
        b.AppendLine("KM123 retains the existing Core GetKaplanMeierPlotData/DTO provider and the native series/clip/censor/CI/legend tail. The change is the Windows analysis/payload overload seam. Common SurvivalReportPolicy.Plot and KaplanMeierCurvePayload.ToCoreData describe the additional GUI snapshot route, not relocated Core calculations. The source retains its accepted worksheet-check/preparation ordering difference; no whole-method equivalence is claimed.\n");
        b.AppendLine("SPC777 maps union/sorted representative axis preparation to the exact univariate projection constructor, sequence intent to SpcChartAxisPoint.New and native category boxing/holder creation to MarshalChartCategories/MarshalAxis. SPC778 maps channel alignment/masks to SpcPanelSeriesProjection.New, and native arrays to MarshalPanel/MarshalChartValues and its explicitly invoked PanelChartData.New. SPC805 maps finite nullable sample preparation plus native nullable-to-Object conversion. SPC814 maps only the replacement nested Windows SharedAxisContext.New. No arbitrary constructor basename is evidence.\n");
        b.AppendLine("PSM Where/order/ThenBy/Y/SMD/label/threshold lambdas map to their exact operators/getters, not an undifferentiated constructor. Helper rows169/170 map to ChartValue/TableValue with finite/NaN/Nothing semantics. Ordinals171/172 retain UNCERTAIN_DIFFERENT_SOURCE: old standalone Nothing handling is not equivalent to the new unguarded helper or inline projection loop. The reachable source operations are traced, but whole-helper equivalence is unproved and requires future-owner characterization. Those source-backed limitations remain visible instead of being erased.\n");
        b.AppendLine("| Ordinal | Disposition | Source-backed operation | Limit |\n|---:|---|---|---|");
        foreach(var row in rows.Where(r=>r["category"]!="UNCHANGED_MATCHED_SOURCE"))b.AppendLine("| "+row["historical_ordinal"]+" | "+row["category"]+" | "+row["reason"].Replace("|","/")+" | "+row.GetValueOrDefault("equivalence_limit","").Replace("|","/")+" |");
        b.AppendLine("\nAll 1,062 historical rows retain exactly one disposition and original order; 1,031 exact rows are retained without recreating their decisions. Current member delta and roadmap maps are unchanged. "+passed+" helper tests pass, including all original 14 and 10 new negative/source-reproducibility regressions. Product suites, native Excel/R, chart capture and scientific goldens remain NOT_RUN/NOT_GOLDEN. P=NO; N1=NO GO; N2=NO; Gate C2=UNMET; zero releases/discharges.\n");
        b.AppendLine("Read the per-operation anchors and hashes in `graphics-lineage-operation-evidence-v2.json`; every target member ID is an actual source declaration in `graphics-lineage-targets-v2.csv`. The live code contains no generic constructor fallback. The old flawed helper is retained only inside the superseded attempt for provenance.\n");
